import Lab from "@/layouts/Lab.astro";
---

<Lab
  title="Privacy Policy | Txchyon"
  description="What data Txchyon collects, why, and the third-party services the site uses."
  canonical="/privacy"
>
  <section class="lab-section first">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">We collect as little as we can, and we don't sell your information.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="lab-section tight prose">
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Newsletter subscriptions:</b> your email address, if you subscribe. Subscriptions are handled by Beehiiv.</li>
      <li><b>Contact messages:</b> the name, email and message you send through the contact form, which is processed by Formspree.</li>
      <li><b>Usage data:</b> anonymous traffic and device data collected by analytics and advertising services (below).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To send the newsletter, only if you subscribed.</li>
      <li>To reply to your messages.</li>
      <li>To understand how the site is used and improve it.</li>
      <li>To comply with legal obligations if required.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Google Analytics</b> and <b>Ahrefs Web Analytics</b> for traffic statistics.</li>
      <li><b>Google AdSense</b> shows ads on article pages and may use cookies to serve and measure ads. See Google's own policies for details and for how to manage ad personalisation.</li>
      <li><b>Beehiiv</b> for newsletter signup and delivery.</li>
      <li><b>Formspree</b> for the contact form.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>These services have their own privacy policies. Some pages also link to exchanges and wallets through affiliate links; those sites are not covered by this policy.</p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Unsubscribe from the newsletter at any time using the link in any email.</li>
      <li>Ask us to delete or show you data you sent us through the contact form.</li>
      <li>Block or clear cookies in your browser; some features may not work without them.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      We take reasonable steps to protect your information, but no online service is completely secure. We also recommend strong
      passwords and two-factor authentication on all of your crypto accounts.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy. Changes will be posted here with a new date.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about privacy? Email <a href="mailto:contact@txchyon.com">contact@txchyon.com</a>.</p>

    <p class="small">Last updated October 23, 2026.</p>
  </section>
</Lab>
